+/*
+    apricorn-oracle — the headless melonDS that produces apricorn traces.
+
+    Patched into melonDS 1.1 by the apricorn project (Phase 2 oracle).
+    Not a frontend: no window, no audio, no JIT, no GDB stub — built
+    against the core-only configuration (see oracle/setup.ps1). The
+    determinism contract is exactly those build flags plus the pinned
+    RTC and frame-indexed execution below.
+
+    It boots a ROM via DirectBoot (no BIOS/firmware dumps needed; the
+    generated firmware and FreeBIOS defaults are deterministic), runs
+    frames with injected input, hashes watched memory regions, and can
+    also run per-function probes (the `C` records) by hijacking the
+    ARM9 at a frame boundary exactly the way arm-runner does on its
+    own interpreter: registers in, step until the PC reaches a sentinel,
+    registers out. On request it also writes both LCDs as PNGs at the
+    end of listed frames (`--shots`) — ground truth for visual review;
+    the trace is byte-identical with or without them.
+
+    All binary inputs are little-endian blobs compiled by the apricorn
+    Rust harness (single source of truth for the text formats); the
+    `*-sha1` header values are passthroughs of the canonical text-file
+    hashes so the comparator can gate producer pairs. The trace text
+    matches crates/apricorn-harness/src/trace.rs byte for byte.
+
+    usage:
+      apricorn-oracle run --rom ROM.nds --out trace.txt
+                         --regions regions.bin [--input input.bin]
+                         [--probes probes.bin] [--frames N] [--rtc ISO]
+                         --input-sha1 HEX --regions-sha1 HEX
+                         [--producer oracle-melonds-1.1]
+                         [--shots F,F,... --shots-dir DIR]
+                         [--gx-shots F,F,... --gx-shots-dir DIR]
+*/
+
